(vector (map (:adr/status "accepted"), (:adr/id "2607100030-kotoba-kami-engine-host-imports.edn"), (:adr/doc_type "adr"), (:adr/normalization-error "The map literal starting with :sha contains 11 form(s). Map literals must contain an even number of forms."), (:adr/body "# ADR-2607100030: kami:engine vocabulary as kotoba host imports — the first game authored in a `.kotoba` file\n\n- **Status**: accepted (implemented & landed 2026-07-10)\n- **Related**: ADR-2607078000 (Track B gpu/math f32 host imports — the\n  precedent this follows), ADR-2607062330/2607062400 (actor:host ABI),\n  ADR-2607022700 (no semantic-authority duplication), ADR-2607082400\n  (mesh_drama_profile — first `.kotoba` app), docs/DEMONSTRATIONS.md\n  (kotoba-lang/kotoba).\n\n## Context\n\n`kotoba-lang/kotoba`'s `docs/DEMONSTRATIONS.md` (landed earlier the same\nday) cataloged every real `.kotoba` artifact and ended on an honest gap:\nplayable game logic ran only in the **kotoba-clj subset** (isekai-network's\n01-netsurvivors, kami-genre-base-systems' 8 genre bases) against the\n`kami:engine/*` 4-module import shape of `kami-script-runtime-rs` /\nwasm-webcomponent's `kami-engine-host.js` — no game had ever been authored\nin a `.kotoba` file, because kotoba's own closed host-import table\n(kotoba-core-contracts) had no game-engine vocabulary.\n\n## Decision\n\nExpose a minimal kami:engine ECS vocabulary through kotoba's own single\n`(module \"kotoba\")` capability-guarded ABI — NOT by adopting the kami-clj\n4-module import shape — following the exact registration path the\ngpu/math Track B imports proved (guest computes, host executes):\n\n1. **kotoba-core-contracts** (`9a2f45e3`): capability `\"kami/engine\"`\n   (id 233, one shared capability for the family, like `\"graph/kotoba\"`\n   covering the kgraph-* quartet) + 13 `kami-*` import descriptors:\n   tick-n, spawn, despawn, set-position!, set-velocity!, get-x, get-y,\n   count-tagged, nearest-tagged, move-tagged-toward!, despawn-within!,\n   axis, rand. Batch ops stand in for per-entity iteration the language\n   deliberately doesn't have; `kami-rand` is the host's SEEDED xorshift64\n   stream (deterministic replay), never the OS RNG (`random-bytes`' job).\n2. **kotoba-lang** (`bed42bc6`): `:host/kami-engine` in\n   `effect-for-kind`, registered simultaneously so guard-call can't\n   reproduce the aiueos/actor:host `:unsupported-kind` runtime-denial gap.\n3. **kotoba** (`a2c69208`): `op->kind` entries; a generic\n   `guarded-host-functions` factored out of `real-host-functions`;\n   **`kotoba.kami-host`** — a deterministic host-owned ECS (entity table,\n   fixed-step Euler integration at 1/60s, tick counter, input axes,\n   seeded xorshift64) driven \"host steps, then calls the guest's 0-arg\n   `main`, once per tick\" (the now-days loop convention — no guest-side\n   loop); **`src/kami_survivors.kotoba`** (+ policy granting only\n   `:kami/engine`) — a survivors-style core loop (ring spawns every 20\n   ticks to a 12 cap, 30 u/s chase, a 90-tick nova burst, axis-steered\n   player); and `test/kotoba/kami_game_test.clj` driving 300 real Chicory\n   ticks with exact pinned entity counts (12 → 8 → 10), axis steering,\n   static admission, and a fail-closed runtime denial without the grant.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- The first game authored directly in a `.kotoba` file exists, compiles\n  through the real emitter, and plays deterministically on Chicory —\n  DEMONSTRATIONS.md's Games section now has an \"authored in `.kotoba`\"\n  entry instead of a future-work sentence.\n- Full kotoba suite green (192 tests / 945 assertions), clj-kondo clean;\n  kotoba-core-contracts and kotoba-lang suites green with the additions.\n- ~~Follow-up (recorded in DEMONSTRATIONS.md): a browser port of\n  `kotoba.kami-host`'s ECS in wasm-webcomponent (hand-JS, `kgraph.js` /\n  `actor-host.js` family) so the same compiled `.wasm` ticks on the\n  browser's native engine the way netsurvivors already does.~~\n  **Done — addendum (same day):** wasm-webcomponent `fe04bd69` ships\n  `src/kami-ecs.js` (hand-JS port; BigInt 64-bit xorshift64 bit-exact\n  with the JVM's long math), `examples/kami-survivors/` (the exact\n  `kotoba wasm emit` binary — 756 bytes, 12 imports, admission-verified —\n  on canvas + requestAnimationFrame, arrow keys/WASD → host axes), and\n  `test/verify-kami-survivors.mjs`, which replays the same 300-tick run\n  on native WebAssembly (V8) and asserts the SAME pinned counts\n  (12 → 8 → 10, player at origin, 15 spawned, x=59 axis check) kotoba's\n  Chicory test pins — count-for-count cross-engine parity on the first\n  run. Full `npm test` (9 verify-*.mjs) green. Real-browser DOM/rAF\n  rendering remains outside the Node test's reach (the repo's documented\n  gap; the Chrome extension was unavailable in this session).\n  kotoba `31263fa8` updates DEMONSTRATIONS.md accordingly.\n- West pins advanced for kotoba / kotoba-core-contracts / kotoba-lang in\n  the same landing.\n\n## Addendum 2 (2026-07-10) — runtime-priority realignment: the host premise is ClojureScript, not the JVM\n\nOwner directive: premise the kami host on kotoba wasm runtime /\nclojurewasm / ClojureScript — not the JVM (the 2026-07-07 repo-wide\nruntime priority). Walking the ladder: the **guest** is already kotoba\nwasm; a **host** cannot be expressed in the `.kotoba` subset (N/A by\ndesign). **clojurewasm is blocked today** — cljw v1.0.1's FFI is\n`wasm/load`+`wasm/call` for import-free modules, with Clojure-provided\nhost imports explicitly deferred to its \"fuller Phase-16 FFI surface\"\n(upstream `docs/examples/wasm/README.edn`, checked 2026-07-10), and this\nguest needs 12 host imports; revisit when Phase-16 lands. **ClojureScript\nadopted**:\n\n- kotoba `367b4a14` — `kami_host.clj` → **`kami_host.cljc`**: fully\n  portable ECS core; xorshift64 reimplemented as ONE 32-bit-pair\n  implementation, bit-identical on JVM longs / cljs int32 ops / nbb SCI;\n  `:cljs` wire layer (`kami-host-imports` for the native\n  `js/WebAssembly` engine); `:clj` Chicory layer kept for the compat\n  suite only. `scripts/verify_kami_survivors_nbb.cljs` (nbb, **no JVM**)\n  drives the checked-in fixture for the same 300 ticks and pins the same\n  counts — green. Also caught: `test_runner.clj`'s fixed namespace list\n  had never included `kotoba.kami-game-test` (the kami suite silently\n  never ran under `-M:test`); registered — now 198 tests / 975\n  assertions, 0 failures.\n- wasm-webcomponent `06316562` — the hand-JS `kami-ecs.js` is retired;\n  it is now **compiled by shadow-cljs** from a thin\n  `src-cljs/kotoba/kami_ecs.cljs` adapter over the **vendored**\n  `kami_host.cljc` (file-for-file from kotoba@367b4a14, `src/vendor`\n  ed25519 convention). One `.cljc` source now serves the JVM compat\n  suite, the nbb script, and the browser/Node ESM. `npm test` green."), (:adr/normalization-status :raw-preserved), (:db/id -1), (:adr/title "ADR-2607100030: kami:engine vocabulary as kotoba host imports — the first game authored in a `.kotoba` file"), (:adr/source-format "edn"), (:adr/raw-edn "{:adr/id \"2607100030\"\n :adr/title \"kami:engine vocabulary as kotoba host imports — the first game authored in a .kotoba file\"\n :adr/status :accepted\n :adr/date \"2026-07-10\"\n :adr/related [\"2607078000-kototama-wasm-gpu-track-b\"\n               \"2607062330-kototama-actor-host-abi\"\n               \"2607062400-wasm-webcomponent-actor-host\"\n               \"2607022700-aiueos-kernel-capabilities\"\n               \"2607082400-mesh-drama-profile-kotoba-port\"]\n\n :gap \"docs/DEMONSTRATIONS.md (kotoba-lang/kotoba) ended on: playable game logic ran only in the kotoba-clj subset (netsurvivors, kami-genre-base-systems) against kami-script-runtime-rs's 4-module kami:engine/* import shape; no game had ever been authored in a .kotoba file because kotoba-core-contracts' closed host-import table had no game-engine vocabulary\"\n\n :decision \"expose a minimal kami:engine ECS vocabulary through kotoba's own single (module \\\"kotoba\\\") capability-guarded ABI (NOT the kami-clj 4-module shape), following the gpu/math Track B registration path (guest computes, host executes)\"\n\n :registration\n {:kotoba-core-contracts {:sha \"9a2f45e333908603b52689479572ba9d4acdf1fa\"\n                          :capability \"kami/engine\" :capability-id 233\n                          :ops '[kami-tick-n kami-spawn kami-despawn\n                                 kami-set-position! kami-set-velocity!\n                                 kami-get-x kami-get-y kami-count-tagged\n                                 kami-nearest-tagged kami-move-tagged-toward!\n                                 kami-despawn-within! kami-axis kami-rand]\n                          :notes \"one shared capability for the family (graph/kotoba precedent); batch ops stand in for per-entity iteration the language deliberately doesn't have; kami-rand = host's SEEDED xorshift64 (deterministic replay), never the OS RNG\"}\n  :kotoba-lang {:sha \"bed42bc6c6598e02e3dfcbba316dfd5666fa2c1d\"\n                :change \":host/kami-engine in effect-for-kind, registered simultaneously so guard-call can't reproduce the aiueos/actor:host :unsupported-kind runtime-denial gap\"}\n  :kotoba {:sha \"a2c692082f9dd4b45f463061990c97a984f9e71e\"\n           :changes [\"op->kind entries for the kami-* family\"\n                     \"wasm-exec: generic guarded-host-functions factored out of real-host-functions\"\n                     \"kotoba.kami-host: deterministic host-owned ECS (entity table, fixed-step Euler 1/60s, tick counter, input axes, seeded xorshift64), 'host steps then calls the guest's 0-arg main once per tick' (now-days loop convention)\"\n                     \"src/kami_survivors.kotoba + policy granting only :kami/engine — THE FIRST GAME AUTHORED DIRECTLY IN A .kotoba FILE (ring spawns every 20 ticks to a 12 cap, 30 u/s chase, 90-tick nova burst, axis-steered player)\"\n                     \"test/kotoba/kami_game_test.clj: 300 real Chicory ticks, exact pinned entity counts 12→8→10 (netsurvivors' parity-by-counts method), axis steering, static admission, fail-closed runtime denial without the grant\"]}}\n\n :verification {:kotoba-suite \"192 tests / 945 assertions, 0 failures; clj-kondo errors 0 warnings 0\"\n                :kotoba-core-contracts-suite \"14 tests / 209 assertions, 0 failures\"\n                :kotoba-lang-suite \"33 tests / 237 assertions, 0 failures\"\n                :determinism \"seeded xorshift64 + fixed-step integration -> same run every time; counts pinned exactly, not flaky\"}\n\n :follow-up []\n\n :addendum-browser-port\n {:date \"2026-07-10\"\n  :wasm-webcomponent {:sha \"fe04bd697ce3d0e8e5894a32868bf593c4270ccc\"\n                      :changes [\"src/kami-ecs.js — hand-JS port of kotoba.kami-host (kgraph.js/actor-host.js family, no build step); xorshift64 in BigInt 64-bit math, bit-exact with the JVM long math\"\n                                \"examples/kami-survivors/ — the exact kotoba wasm emit binary (756 bytes, 12 imports, package-admission verified) on canvas + requestAnimationFrame, arrow keys/WASD wired to the host-owned MoveX/MoveY axes\"\n                                \"test/verify-kami-survivors.mjs — replays the same 300-tick run (seed 7) on native WebAssembly (V8) and asserts the SAME pinned counts kotoba's Chicory test pins: 12→8→10, player at origin, 15 spawned, x=59 axis check — count-for-count cross-engine parity on the first run\"]}\n  :kotoba-docs {:sha \"31263fa81e16cf1ac3f02b9c93a8b44ff7c4a337\"\n                :change \"DEMONSTRATIONS.md: browser demo recorded, follow-up sentence replaced\"}\n  :verification \"npm test green (all 9 verify-*.mjs). Real-browser DOM/rAF rendering remains outside the Node test's reach (the repo's documented gap; Chrome extension unavailable this session)\"}\n\n :addendum-runtime-priority-realignment\n {:date \"2026-07-10\"\n  :directive \"owner: the kami host must be premised on kotoba wasm runtime / clojurewasm / ClojureScript — not the JVM (CLAUDE.md 2026-07-07 runtime priority)\"\n  :ladder-walked\n  {:kotoba-wasm \"the GUEST already is kotoba wasm; the HOST cannot be expressed in the .kotoba subset (no data structures / no hosting surface) — N/A by design, recorded in the ns docstring\"\n   :clojurewasm \"BLOCKED today: cljw v1.0.1's FFI is wasm/load+wasm/call for import-free modules; Clojure-provided host imports are explicitly the future 'fuller Phase-16 FFI surface' (upstream docs/examples/wasm/README.edn, checked 2026-07-10) and kami_survivors.wasm needs 12 host imports. Revisit when Phase-16 lands\"\n   :clojurescript \"ADOPTED as the host premise\"}\n  :kotoba {:sha \"367b4a141b94f0c2dce78e822b85b2fc28248617\"\n           :changes [\"kami_host.clj → kami_host.cljc: portable ECS core; xorshift64 reimplemented as ONE 32-bit-pair implementation (u32/xor64/shl64/shr64 + 16-bit-limb pair-mod), bit-identical on JVM longs / cljs int32 ops / nbb SCI\"\n                     \":cljs wire layer kami-host-imports (native js/WebAssembly import object); :clj Chicory layer kept for the compat suite only\"\n                     \"scripts/verify_kami_survivors_nbb.cljs — nbb (no JVM) drives the checked-in fixture 300 ticks, same pinned counts: GREEN\"\n                     \"test/kotoba/fixtures/kami_survivors.wasm checked in (deterministic emit, byte-identical to wasm-webcomponent's copy) + fixture-in-sync test\"\n                     \"BUG FOUND: test_runner.clj's fixed namespace list had never included kotoba.kami-game-test — the kami suite had silently never run under -M:test (constant 192 tests through the original landing). Registered; now 198 tests / 975 assertions, 0 failures\"]}\n  :wasm-webcomponent {:sha \"063165620870eec043a3f2035952d9ec3d881f0f\"\n                      :changes [\"hand-JS src/kami-ecs.js RETIRED; now compiled by shadow-cljs :kami-ecs (:target :esm, kami-engine-host/ADR-2607078000 precedent) from src-cljs/kotoba/kami_ecs.cljs (thin JS-facing adapter, same createKamiEcs/kamiHostImports API)\"\n                                \"src-cljs/vendor/kotoba/kami_host.cljc vendored file-for-file from kotoba@367b4a14 (src/vendor ed25519 convention, provenance header) — ONE .cljc source now serves JVM compat, nbb, and the browser/Node ESM\"\n                                \"npm test green (all 9 verify-*.mjs incl. the pinned kami-survivors parity run)\"]}}\n\n :west-pins-advanced {:kotoba \"1dbcc2eb→a2c69208→31263fa8→367b4a14\"\n                      :kotoba-core-contracts \"bc327f29→9a2f45e3\"\n                      :kotoba-lang \"ec360a80→bed42bc6\"\n                      :wasm-webcomponent \"ee8d4ea4→fe04bd69→06316562\"}}\n")))